.TH BMAP-SEND 1 "2026-11-07" "bmaptool" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bmap-send \- send an image and its bmap file to a remote host
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bmap-send
[\-P \fIPORT\fR] [\-y] [\-\-verify | \-\-no-verify] \fIIMAGE\fR \fIDESTINATION\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fIbmap-send\fR transfers a local image file and its bmap file to a remote host
using \fBscp\fR. The bmap file must be generated beforehand with
\fIbmaptool create\fR and is expected locally as \fIIMAGE\fR.bmap.
.PP
\fIDESTINATION\fR has the form [user@]host:/path/to/image.raw. If the remote
path ends with "/", it is treated as a directory and the local image name is
appended. The remote bmap file is stored next to the image as
/path/to/image.raw.bmap.
.PP
The image is transferred first and the bmap file second, so the remote side
never sees a bmap file that refers to an incomplete image. File timestamps are
preserved with \fBscp -p\fR.
.PP
By default the remote copy is not verified; the transfer only sends the data and
the bmap file. Use \fB\-\-verify\fR to run \fIbmaptool verify\fR on the remote
host after the transfer.
.PP
If the source image modification time differs from the time recorded in the
bmap, \fIbmap-send\fR prints a warning and asks
"Continue? [y/N]". Only "y" or "yes" continues; any other answer or end of
input aborts the transfer. This catches an image that was modified after its
bmap was created.
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\-h, \-\-help
.RS 2
Print short help text and exit.
.RE
.PP
\-P, \-\-port \fIPORT\fR
.RS 2
Use \fIPORT\fR for the SSH connection.
.RE
.PP
\-y, \-\-yes
.RS 2
Continue without prompting when the source image mtime differs from the bmap.
.RE
.PP
\-\-verify
.RS 2
Run \fIbmaptool verify\fR on the remote host after the transfer. The remote host
must have \fIbmaptool\fR installed.
.RE
.PP
\-\-no-verify
.RS 2
Do not verify the image on the remote host (default).
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
\fIbmap-send\fR image.raw user@host:/data/image.raw
.RS 2
Send image.raw to /data/image.raw and its bmap to /data/image.raw.bmap.
.RE
.PP
\fIbmap-send\fR \-\-verify image.raw user@host:/data/image.raw
.RS 2
Send the files and run "\fIbmaptool\fR verify /data/image.raw.bmap" on the
remote host afterwards.
.RE
.PP
\fIbmap-send\fR \-y image.raw user@host:/data/
.RS 2
Send the files into the remote /data/ directory without prompting if the source
image mtime changed.
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.PP
0 on success, 1 on error or when the transfer is aborted.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bmaptool (1)
